{
  "sn36.6:0.1": "Linked Discourses 36.6 ",
  "sn36.6:0.2": "1. With Verses ",
  "sn36.6:0.3": "An Arrow ",
  "sn36.6:1.1": "“Mendicants, an unlearned ordinary person feels pleasant, painful, and neutral feelings. ",
  "sn36.6:1.2": "A learned noble disciple also feels pleasant, painful, and neutral feelings. ",
  "sn36.6:1.3": "What, then, is the difference between a learned noble disciple and an ordinary unlearned person?” ",
  "sn36.6:1.4": "“Our teachings are rooted in the Buddha. …” ",
  "sn36.6:1.5": "“When an unlearned ordinary person experiences painful physical feelings they sorrow and wail and lament, beating their breast and falling into confusion. ",
  "sn36.6:1.6": "They experience two feelings: ",
  "sn36.6:1.7": "physical and mental. ",
  "sn36.6:1.8": "It’s like a person who is struck with an arrow, ",
  "sn36.6:1.9": "only to be struck with a second arrow. ",
  "sn36.6:1.10": "That person experiences the feeling of two arrows. ",
  "sn36.6:1.11": "In the same way, when an unlearned ordinary person experiences painful physical feelings they sorrow and wail and lament, beating their breast and falling into confusion. ",
  "sn36.6:1.12": "They experience two feelings: ",
  "sn36.6:1.13": "physical and mental. ",
  "sn36.6:1.14": "When they’re touched by painful feeling, they resist it. ",
  "sn36.6:1.15": "The underlying tendency for aversion toward painful feeling underlies that. ",
  "sn36.6:1.16": "When touched by painful feeling they look forward to enjoying sensual pleasures.